# Student Management System

A full-stack CRUD web application built per the SOP:
**Plain HTML/CSS/JavaScript frontend + Django REST Framework backend + SQLite database.**

Manages student records (roll number, name, email, phone, department, year)
with Create, Read, Update, Delete, search, and filtering.

---

## 1. Architecture

```
Browser (HTML/CSS/JS) --fetch()--> Django REST Framework API --ORM--> SQLite
```

- **Frontend**: `frontend/` — static HTML/CSS/JS, no build step, no framework.
- **Backend**: `backend/` — Django project `student_management` with one app, `students`.
- **Database**: SQLite by default (`backend/db.sqlite3`), swappable to PostgreSQL/MySQL.

## 2. Project Structure

```
student-management-system/
├── backend/
│   ├── manage.py
│   ├── requirements.txt
│   ├── student_management/      # project settings, urls, wsgi/asgi
│   └── students/                 # the CRUD app
│       ├── models.py             # Student model
│       ├── serializers.py        # DRF serializer + validation
│       ├── views.py              # ModelViewSet (CRUD + search/filter)
│       ├── urls.py               # /api/students/ routes
│       ├── admin.py              # Django admin registration
│       └── migrations/
├── frontend/
│   ├── index.html
│   ├── style.css
│   └── script.js
└── README.md
```

## 3. Prerequisites

- Python 3.9+
- pip

## 4. Backend Setup

```bash
cd backend
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate        # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate

pip install -r requirements.txt

python manage.py migrate        # creates db.sqlite3 and applies the included migration
python manage.py createsuperuser  # optional, for /admin/ access

python manage.py runserver
```

The API is now running at `http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/students/`.
The Django admin is at `http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/`.

> Note: an initial migration is already included in `students/migrations/0001_initial.py`,
> so `migrate` alone is enough. If you change `models.py`, run
> `python manage.py makemigrations students` first.

## 5. Frontend Setup

The frontend is plain static files — no build step required. Serve it with
any simple HTTP server (opening `index.html` directly via `file://` also
works, but a local server avoids some browser quirks):

```bash
cd frontend
python -m http.server 5500
```

Then open **http://127.0.0.1:5500** in your browser. Make sure the Django
backend (step 4) is running at the same time — the frontend calls
`http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/students/` (configurable at the top of `script.js`
via the `API_BASE` constant).

CORS is enabled in `settings.py` (`django-cors-headers`) so the frontend,
served from a different port, can call the API.

## 6. REST API Reference

| Operation | Method | Endpoint | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| List | GET | `/api/students/` | Supports `?search=`, `?department=`, `?year=` |
| Retrieve | GET | `/api/students/{id}/` | |
| Create | POST | `/api/students/` | JSON body, see fields below |
| Update | PUT | `/api/students/{id}/` | Full update |
| Partial update | PATCH | `/api/students/{id}/` | Partial update |
| Delete | DELETE | `/api/students/{id}/` | |

**Student fields**

| Field | Type | Rules |
|---|---|---|
| `roll_number` | string | required, unique |
| `name` | string | required, min 2 chars |
| `email` | string | required, valid email, unique |
| `phone` | string | optional, 7–15 digits with optional leading `+` |
| `department` | string | one of `CSE, ECE, MECH, CIVIL, EEE, IT, OTHER` |
| `year` | integer | required, 1–6 |

Server-side validation runs even though the frontend also validates
client-side. Validation errors come back as `400 Bad Request` with a JSON
`errors` object keyed by field name, which the frontend maps directly onto
the form.

### Example: create a student (curl)

```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/students/ \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"roll_number":"CSE001","name":"Asha Rao","email":"asha@example.com","phone":"+919876543210","department":"CSE","year":2}'
```

## 7. Testing Checklist (per SOP §10)

Use Postman or curl against the endpoints above to verify:

- [ ] Create with valid data → `201`, record appears in `/api/students/`
- [ ] Create with missing required field → `400` with field error
- [ ] Create with duplicate `roll_number` or `email` → `400` uniqueness error
- [ ] Read all → `200`, list matches database
- [ ] Read one with invalid id → `404`
- [ ] Update with valid id/data → `200`, values change
- [ ] Update with invalid id → `404`
- [ ] Delete with valid id → `200`, record removed
- [ ] Delete with invalid id → `404`
- [ ] Search (`?search=`) and department filter (`?department=`) return the right subset
- [ ] Frontend form shows client-side + server-side validation errors correctly
- [ ] Frontend still gives a clear error message if the backend is stopped

## 8. Security Notes

- `DJANGO_SECRET_KEY` and `DJANGO_DEBUG` are read from environment
  variables in `settings.py` — set these explicitly (and `DEBUG=False`,
  a real secret key, and a locked-down `ALLOWED_HOSTS`/CORS origin list)
  before deploying anywhere public.
- No credentials are hard-coded in source.
- All database access goes through the Django ORM (parameterized queries).

## 9. Possible Future Enhancements

- Authentication (login) so only authorized staff can modify records
- Pagination controls in the frontend UI (the API already paginates)
- CSV export/import of student records
- Attendance or grades as a related model
